    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.indentscope\n\n### Description\n\nI love the animation and look of mini.indentscope but one thing that really stops me fully switch from indent-blankline is the ability to ignore the first indent `show_first_level_indent = false`.\r\n\r\nI work in sometimes large typescript react files where most of the files is indented one level which makes the animation take too long (I have it sped up for this case) and doesn't provide useful information!\r\n\r\nIs it possible to add an option to ignore this here?",
    "closed_at": "2023-05-27T07:57:32Z",
