        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "My config is very simple for speeding these up, with just hard stops based on my usage:\r\n```\r\n      require(\"mini.indentscope\").setup({\r\n        draw = {\r\n          delay = 500,\r\n          animation = function(_n, total)\r\n            if total > 40 then\r\n              return 0\r\n            elseif total > 30 then\r\n              return 2\r\n            elseif total > 20 then\r\n              return 5\r\n            end\r\n            return 15\r\n          end,\r\n        },\r\n      })\r\n```\r\nThis just speeds up the line rendering but I would still really like to have no line at all for the first level.. \r\n\r\nmy own random thought: perhaps the animation function could receive the indent level as well and be able to return a table, something like `{wait: 10, symbol: \"\"}` then you could have different symbols at each level including blank (or nil?)",
